          `Ab hum "what-if" sawaal poochhte hain — yahi woh sawaal hain jo interviewer poochhta hai.

**What if: MAC address na hota?** Tab ek network ke andar computer ek doosre ko pehchan hi nahi paate. IP address se kaam chal sakta hai, par IP address badalta rehta hai — jab aap ghar se office jaate ho, toh IP badal jaata hai. MAC address device ki permanent pehchan hai, isliye switch ko pata chalta hai ki kaunsi cable par kaunsa device hai. Bina MAC ke switch ko har frame sab ko bhejna padta — network bahut slow ho jaata.

**What if: switch na hota, sirf hub hota?** Tab har frame har computer ko jaata. 10 computer wale office mein har computer ko 10 guna data milta — jismein se 9 hissa uska nahi hota. Network slow ho jaata aur security bhi khatam ho jaati, kyunki koi bhi kisi ka data padh sakta. Switch ne hi aaj ke tez aur secure LAN ko mumkin banaya hai.

**What if: error check na hota?** Tab kharab frame bhi upar ki layers tak pahuncha jaata, aur app ko kharab data milta. Aapki photo download hoti toh beech mein kharab hissa dikhta, aur aapko pata bhi nahi chalta ki kahan kharabi hai. CRC yeh pakka karta hai ki upar sirf sahi frame jaaye — kharab frame neeche hi phenk diya jaata hai.

**What if: framing na hoti?** Tab receiver ko pata hi nahi chalta ki ek frame kahan khatam aur doosra kahan shuru hota hai. Saara data ek lambi stream ban jaata, aur receiver use samajh nahi pata. Framing hi data ko tukdon mein baant ti hai taaki har tukda alag se check aur deliver ho sake. Neeche wala code parity bit ka dry run dikhata hai — ek bit ki galti kaise pakdi jaati hai.`,
          `Now let us ask "what-if" questions — these are exactly the questions interviewers ask.

**What if there was no MAC address?** Then computers inside one network could not recognize each other at all. An IP address could do the job, but it keeps changing — when you go from home to office, the IP changes. The MAC address is the permanent identity of a device, so the switch knows which device sits on which cable. Without MAC, the switch would have to send every frame to everyone — the network would become very slow.

**What if there was no switch, only a hub?** Then every frame would go to every computer. In an office with 10 computers, each computer would receive 10 times the data — 9 parts of which are not for it. The network would slow down, and security would end too, because anyone could read anyone's data. The switch is what made today's fast and secure LAN possible.

**What if there was no error check?** Then damaged frames would also reach the upper layers, and apps would receive damaged data. If you downloaded a photo, a damaged part would show in the middle, and you would never know where the damage was. CRC makes sure only correct frames go up — damaged frames are thrown away below.

**What if there was no framing?** Then the receiver would never know where one frame ends and the next begins. All the data would become one long stream, and the receiver could not make sense of it. Framing is what splits data into pieces so each piece can be checked and delivered separately. The code below shows a parity bit dry run — how a one-bit error is caught.`
