      'A network gets its name from how big it is: a LAN for a home or office, a MAN for a city, and a WAN for a country or the world. In this article you will learn the topologies — bus, star, ring, and mesh — with their link counts, their strengths and weaknesses, and how VLANs split one switch into separate logical networks, all counted by hand.'
