          `Network mein data ek device se doosre device tak khud nahi pahunchta — beech mein **devices** use forward karte hain. Har device ka kaam alag hai aur woh OSI model ki alag layer par kaam karta hai. Sabse neeche **repeater aur hub Layer 1 (Physical)** par hain — woh sirf signal ko aage badhate hain, samajhte kuch nahi. **Switch Layer 2 (Data Link)** par hai — woh MAC address padhta hai. **Router Layer 3 (Network)** par hai — woh IP address padhta hai. **Gateway Layer 3 aur uske upar** kaam karta hai — woh do alag networks ko jodta hai. **Modem Layer 1** par hai — woh digital signal ko analog mein badalta hai.

Socho data ek letter hai. Repeater woh hai jo dheemi awaaz ko dobara zor se bol de. Hub woh postman hai jo letter ki copy har ghar mein daal de. Switch woh smart postman hai jo sirf sahi ghar mein letter daalta hai. Router woh hai jo letter ko ek sheher se doosre sheher bhejta hai. Gateway woh translator hai jo do alag bhasha bolne wale shehron ke beech baat karwata hai. Modem woh hai jo letter ko ek medium se doosre medium mein badal de.

Har device ko uske layer se yaad rakho: **repeater/hub = Layer 1, switch = Layer 2, router = Layer 3**. Interview mein yahi sawaal sabse pehle aata hai.`,
          `In a network, data does not reach from one device to another on its own — **devices** in the middle forward it. Each device has a different job and works on a different layer of the OSI model. At the bottom, the **repeater and hub sit on Layer 1 (Physical)** — they only push the signal forward and understand nothing. The **switch sits on Layer 2 (Data Link)** — it reads the MAC address. The **router sits on Layer 3 (Network)** — it reads the IP address. The **gateway works on Layer 3 and above** — it joins two different networks. The **modem sits on Layer 1** — it changes a digital signal into an analog one.

Imagine data is a letter. The repeater is the person who repeats a faint voice loudly. The hub is the postman who drops a copy of the letter at every house. The switch is the smart postman who drops the letter only at the right house. The router is the one who sends the letter from one city to another. The gateway is the translator who lets two cities speaking different languages talk. The modem is the one who changes the letter from one medium to another.

Remember each device by its layer: **repeater/hub = Layer 1, switch = Layer 2, router = Layer 3**. Interviews ask exactly this first.`
